<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carlsbad Decrees</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1819</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Carlsbad Decrees were measures agreed by German states at Carlsbad in August 1819 at the urging of Metternich and adopted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-convention-german-confederation">Federal Diet of the German Confederation</a> in September. Prompted by the murder of the writer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/august-von-kotzebue">August von Kotzebue</a> by a student, they banned the nationalist student fraternities, imposed press censorship and placed universities under supervision. They became a symbol of the repression of the Restoration era.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carlsbad-decrees.jpg" alt="Carlsbad Decrees" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hstoops · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:German_Conservatism_Flags_Symbol.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
